WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.211
Imagine taking a complex testing workflow and moving

00:00:04.211 --> 00:00:07.438
parts of it into channels so small that fluid

00:00:07.438 --> 00:00:08.083
behaviour

00:00:08.083 --> 00:00:10.054
becomes a design constraint.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.670
Specimen collection, sample transport and preparation

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:18.889
can

00:00:18.889 --> 00:00:22.476
determine whether a miniature diagnostic device is

00:00:22.476 --> 00:00:22.979
useful.

00:00:27.217 --> 00:00:31.049
Microfluidic systems can organise small volumes and

00:00:31.049 --> 00:00:34.724
reactions, but sensitivity and specificity still

00:00:34.724 --> 00:00:35.183
depend

00:00:35.183 --> 00:00:36.987
on the biological assay.

00:00:41.842 --> 00:00:45.484
Finding an analytical signal requires distinguishing

00:00:45.484 --> 00:00:49.266
target detection, contamination, false results and the

00:00:49.266 --> 00:00:50.596
clinical situation.

00:00:55.008 --> 00:00:59.009
Manufacturability, reliable reagents, operator burden

00:00:59.009 --> 00:00:59.235
and

00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:02.482
clinical validation decide whether a clever

00:01:02.482 --> 00:01:03.313
microsystem

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:04.426
becomes useful.

00:01:09.092 --> 00:01:13.227
The 2021 review surveys microfluidic approaches to

00:01:13.227 --> 00:01:17.611
respiratory-virus detection and the evidence required

00:01:17.611 --> 00:01:19.513
beyond the chip itself.
